# Commit Message Convention

All git commit messages in this repository MUST follow
[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): a lowercase type
prefix, an optional scope, and a concise imperative summary.

## Format

```text
<type>(<optional-scope>): <summary>

<optional body>
```

- Type is required and lowercase. Allowed types:
  - `feat` — a new feature
  - `fix` — a bug fix
  - `test` — adding or improving tests only
  - `docs` — documentation only
  - `refactor` — code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
  - `perf` — performance improvement
  - `chore` — build, deps, tooling, or housekeeping
  - `ci` — CI/CD configuration changes
- Scope is optional; use the affected module when helpful (e.g. `doi_query`,
  `word2img`, `ui`, `registry`, `build`).
- Summary is imperative and concise (no trailing period).
- Write in English. Do NOT use an `FM-xxx` (or any Jira-style) prefix.
- Use a body (after a blank line) with `-` bullets for multi-part changes.

## Examples

```text
test: add FakePage harness for UI wiring and boot coverage
fix(doi_query): stop button now cancels the batch immediately
refactor(registry): register built-in tools via a single explicit path
ci: add Ruff lint and a py3.9/3.12 test matrix
```
